WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.661 --> 00:00:01.960
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:04.253
- I see color as a form of communication.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.740
I feel like it tells a story.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.170
When I look at colors like in a painting,

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:12.503
I think automatically,
can I put that on a head?

00:00:12.503 --> 00:00:15.086
(upbeat music)

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:23.400
My name is Daniel Moon,
and I'm a hair colorist.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.060
I first started getting into hair

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.140
when I was in the Marine Corps.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:30.040
I barbered myself and other friends.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.530
I was granted permission to exit

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.473
the Marine Corps to go to hair school.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:37.621
Being so restricted in the military,

00:00:37.621 --> 00:00:40.810
I think getting out of
it, there were no limits.

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.020
Restriction was enforced on me,

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.715
so when it came to creating,

00:00:44.715 --> 00:00:47.970
I had a vow that I'd never restrict myself

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.610
from doing something that
I felt like I wanted to

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.310
and somehow came up with this magic

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:53.390
way of coloring hair.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.400
So freehand hair coloring is looking

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.310
at the head as a canvas.

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:03.480
Whether it's short hair or long hair,

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.000
being able to just paint on it

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.943
as if it was a sculpture.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:12.570
I find inspiration everywhere.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:14.590
I look to the art world;

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:18.960
I look to the magazine
world; I look in books;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.323
I look where people don't
think about looking.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.130
When I'm choosing colors and designs

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:26.340
I imagine like a checkerboard.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.307
This purple is here, this red is here.

00:01:28.307 --> 00:01:30.700
Can I connect this color to that color?

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.550
I'm looking at it from every angle.

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.460
Top, bottom, left, right,

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.780
and then just playing with those

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.400
different kind of shapes.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:38.820
I don't think about being different

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.000
from other hair stylists.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.446
I create work that is different for me;

00:01:42.446 --> 00:01:45.149
it's different from my last piece.

00:01:45.149 --> 00:01:47.566
(calm music)

00:01:50.697 --> 00:01:52.620
I think people dye their hair to have fun-

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.063
to create a persona that's fun to live in.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:57.740
Did some big color changes

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:00.625
and had some great
collaborations with Madonna,

00:02:00.625 --> 00:02:05.625
Katy Perry, Nicole
Richie, and Zoe Kravitz.

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:08.250
The work that I create is temporary,

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.900
and that is a romantic thing.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.997
Because it fades away, hair grows out,

00:02:12.997 --> 00:02:17.380
I can spend three hours,
six hours on a piece,

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:18.450
and then it could walk out the door,

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.070
and then it's never seen again.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.734
I like that it's an art
form that washes away.

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:25.150
I'd like to just continue on creating

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:26.840
and just making something that

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.136
I've never seen before.

00:02:28.136 --> 00:02:30.719
(upbeat music)

